## JsonLiteralQuoteStyle

**Severity:** error | **Type:** LiquidHtml

Inline object and array literals in platformOS Liquid (e.g. `{% raw %}{% assign a = {"a": 5} %}{% endraw %}`) must be valid JSON. Single-quoted strings are not valid JSON, so this check reports any single-quoted string used inside an inline object or array literal — whether as a key or as a value.

Single-quoted strings outside of object/array literals (e.g. `{% raw %}{% assign s = 'hello' %}{% endraw %}`) are perfectly fine and are not reported.

## Examples

### &#x2717; Incorrect Code Example (Avoid using this):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% assign user = {'name': 'Anne'} %}
{% assign ids = ['a', 'b', 'c'] %}
{% assign mixed = {"count": 1, "label": 'items'} %}
{% endraw %}
```

### &#x2713; Correct Code Example (Use this instead):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% assign user = {"name": "Anne"} %}
{% assign ids = ["a", "b", "c"] %}
{% assign mixed = {"count": 1, "label": "items"} %}

{% comment %}Single quotes outside JSON literals are fine:{% endcomment %}
{% assign greeting = 'hello' %}
{% endraw %}
```

## Configuration

The default configuration for this check:

```yaml
JsonLiteralQuoteStyle:
  enabled: true
  severity: error
```

## Disabling This Check

This check should not be disabled — single-quoted strings inside inline object/array literals are not valid JSON.

## Autofixing

This check supports automatic fixing. The fix replaces each single-quoted string with its double-quoted JSON equivalent (escaping the content where needed).
